# Appendix B — Proposed Media Plan + Proposed Build Sheets

## Planning basis and guardrails

This is an optimisation and expansion plan for the mature ErgoWorks Consulting program—not a greenfield launch.

| Item | Verified baseline |
|---|---|
| Google Ads account | `9258098368` |
| Focus campaign | Search campaign `700072710`, ErgoWorks Consulting |
| Current bidding | Maximize Conversions, no target CPA; standard strategy, not portfolio |
| Existing investment | Approximately A$40,000 trailing 12 months |
| Observed monthly range | Approximately A$3.0k–A$4.7k; A$4,246 last 30 days |
| Last-30-day delivery | 4,540 impressions, 407 clicks, 26 reported conversions |
| Estimated real leads | Approximately 20 last 30 days |
| Provisional real-lead CPA | A$4,246 ÷ 20 = **A$212.30** |
| Current social activity | Zero paid social; three Organic Social sessions and no key events in GA4 over the last 90 days |
| Landing-page state | Paid traffic currently reaches generic WordPress service pages |
| Paused campaigns | PMax `16143562968`; Display Remarketing `843760968` |
| Measurement issue | Newsletter and soft actions are included among primary/reported conversions; no qualified-lead import |
| Shared-account risk | Consulting and Physiotherapy coexist in account `9258098368` and require campaign-level isolation |

All recommendations are proposed only. No live-account changes are authorised by this plan.

### Mandatory pre-launch conditions

- Demote newsletter signup and inappropriate soft actions from primary optimisation.
- Isolate Consulting conversion goals, reporting, audiences and campaign negatives from Physiotherapy.
- Use a dedicated ErgoWorks Consulting Meta Pixel/Dataset and properly scoped GA4/GTM implementation, separate from ErgoEquip and Biosymm.
- Implement a CMP and **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, with separate enquiry and marketing consent.
- Complete an Australian privacy review before activating the landing page, Meta Pixel/CAPI, CRM audiences or offline conversion uploads.
- Do not collect injury details, symptoms, diagnoses or other health information in advertising forms.
- Use only controllable-output claims. Do not claim guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance or quantified claims reduction.
- Any awards, Danone reference, client logos, “ASX 100” statement or 5.0/63-review claim remains **client sign-off required** and cannot enter ads or landing pages until verified.
- Wherever offered, the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot must carry the adjacent statement: **“Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.”** If the format cannot carry it, that format must not mention the Snapshot.

### Canonical funnel and bidding map

| Funnel stage | Canonical event | Source of truth | Google bidding treatment | Meta bidding treatment |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Snapshot request | `snapshot_request` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
| Direct enquiry | `direct_enquiry` | CRM-confirmed form submission | Initial Primary | Initial website `Lead` optimisation event |
| Call connected | `call_connected` | Call-tracking platform | Secondary | Reporting only |
| Qualified call | `qualified_call` | CRM/call disposition applying W-Audit rule | Primary only via qualified import once reliable | Send through CAPI; optimisation only after reliable volume |
| Qualified lead | `lead_qualified` | CRM stage | Secondary while validated; future Primary | Future `QualifiedLead`/conversion-leads optimisation signal |
| Proposal | `proposal_sent` | CRM stage | Secondary | CAPI reporting/custom audience |
| Won | `closed_won` | CRM finance-approved stage | Value-bearing secondary initially | CAPI value event and audience exclusion |

Snapshot booked and held are CRM stages only, not platform events.

Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only.

## Proposed channel roles

The 70/20/10 framework is a strategic overlay, not a mandate to underfund platforms below their delivery requirements.

| Overlay | Channel | Proposed role | Evidence and constraint |
|---|---|---|---|
| Proven — 70% | Google Search | Preserve and improve mature demand capture; strengthen Manual Handling Training, care-sector, online/refresher, assessment and consultant coverage; establish Brand protection | Search already produces approximately 20 real leads per month. AU volume includes `manual handling training` at 2,700 searches/month, a care-sector cluster at approximately 780 searches/month, and a certificate/course demand head of approximately 3,400+ searches/month whose buyer type remains unclassified |
| Greenfield demand-generation / TOFU pilot — target ~20% steady-state share once earned | Meta | Create demand among organisational buyers; educate, qualify and retarget traffic into the dedicated conversion landing page | Meta is greenfield for ErgoWorks. Use organisational messaging, creative qualification, interests, qualified-lead lookalikes and retargeting—not job-title targeting; it earns the ~20% share only after showing promise |
| Testing — 10% | PMax plus remarketing | Evaluate incremental reach only after measurement and landing-page remediation | PMax requires at least A$50/day, or A$1,500 per 30-day planning month. A normal 10% slice is insufficient at current spend |
| Unfunded future pilot | LinkedIn ABM | Reach named accounts using professional targeting when economics justify the premium | No share of the current media budget; entry criteria apply |

Search remains the revenue engine. The 2026-07-13 Ahrefs AU pull confirms every volume in the account-snapshot table below exactly; these figures are verified demand indicators, not forecasts of available clicks or leads. CPC figures retain the source caveat: Ahrefs values are treated as approximate A$ planning estimates, not observed Google Ads CPCs (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §1):

| AU keyword | Monthly volume | KD | CPC |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `manual handling training` | 2,700 | 22 | A$1.00 |
| `ergonomic assessment` | 400 | 0 | A$2.50 |
| `ergonomic consultant` | 200 | 26 | A$5.00 |
| `manual handling training sydney` | 200 | 15 | A$1.10 |
| `home office ergonomic assessment` | 100 | Not available | A$5.00 |
| `office ergonomic assessment` | 70 | 0 | A$1.80 |
| `workplace ergonomic assessment` | 60 | 2 | A$1.50 |
| `workstation assessment` | 50 | Not available | A$1.90 |
| `ergonomic assessment software` | 40 | Not available | Not available |
| `train the trainer manual handling` | 10 | Not available | A$1.10 |

`ergonomic assessment software` is retained in this verification table because it was part of the original snapshot, but the verified intent is software/SaaS and it is an exclusion candidate—not a positive ErgoAssess keyword—unless later Search Terms Report evidence proves relevant consulting intent.

## Proposed budget scenarios

All monthly calculations use a **30-day planning month**. Actual calendar-month invoices will vary with pacing and month length.

The scenarios are anchored to both the approximately **A$40,000 trailing-12-month Search investment** and the observed **A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range**, using the verified last-30-day spend of **A$4,246** as the exact planning baseline.

For Meta planning, the initial optimisation event is website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only—not raw Search enquiries or soft actions. No observed Meta lead-entry CPA exists; the provisional range below is derived from the lower-friction Snapshot path and remains assumption-based:

- **Assumption 1:** a Snapshot Request costs **25%–40%** of the A$212.30 Search raw-enquiry CPL because it is a free, lower-friction lead magnet.
- **Assumption 2:** A$212.30 × 25%–40% produces a provisional Snapshot-request CPA range of **A$53.08–A$84.92**.
- **Planning anchor:** use the conservative upper end, **A$84.92 per Snapshot Request**, until Meta produces clean observed data.
- **Upper-bound sensitivity only:** A$212.30 remains a conservative raw-enquiry-CPL sensitivity; it is not the Meta target-CPA anchor.
- The commercial target remains not assessable pending average contract value, contribution margin and qualified-lead rate.

### Scenario 1 — Current-budget reallocation; PMax parked

This scenario holds total media at the verified last-30-day spend. Meta receives its delivery floor, so the resulting mix cannot reach 70/20/10.

| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Google Search | A$4,246 − A$600 | **A$3,646** | **85.87%** |
| Meta | A$20/day × 30 | **A$600** | **14.13%** |
| PMax plus remarketing | Parked | **A$0** | **0.00%** |
| **Total** |  | **A$4,246** | **100.00%** |

Decision: use only if the budget must remain flat. Meta’s A$600 budget passes both the delivery floor and the provisional A$424.60 learning-budget check for one ad set. Treat this as a controlled baseline-establishment test because the Snapshot-request CPA is assumption-based and commercial lead economics remain unknown.

The A$600 must sit in **one consolidated prospecting ad set**. A separately funded remarketing ad set would push each ad set below the A$20/day floor; therefore, build remarketing audiences during this scenario but park paid retargeting until volume and budget support it.

### Scenario 2 — Minimum-viable Meta added on top

This scenario protects the existing Search run-rate and adds the Meta delivery floor, which is higher than the provisional learning-budget requirement.

| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **87.62%** |
| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **12.38%** |
| PMax plus remarketing | Parked | **A$0.00** | **0.00%** |
| **Total** |  | **A$4,846.00** | **100.00%** |

Decision: preferred minimum launch scenario. It protects the existing Search run-rate while funding one Meta ad set above both sufficiency checks. It does not achieve the intended 80/20 active-channel mix; that overlay should not override the current event-level planning assumptions or platform floor.

Meta receives **A$20/day** over 30 days. Keep this in one consolidated prospecting ad set initially. Build retargeting audiences but do not fragment the budget.

### Scenario 3 — Minimum-viable Meta plus PMax at its floor

This scenario keeps the existing Search baseline, adds minimum-viable Meta and funds PMax at A$50/day.

| Channel | Calculation | Proposed 30-day budget | Actual share |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **66.91%** |
| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **9.45%** |
| PMax | A$50/day × 30 | **A$1,500.00** | **23.64%** |
| Display remarketing | Parked initially | **A$0.00** | **0.00%** |
| **Total** |  | **A$6,346.00** | **100.00%** |

Decision: use only after the measurement and landing-page gates pass. Platform floors materially override 70/20/10: PMax becomes 23.64% rather than 10%, while Search is 66.91% and Meta is 9.45%.

Do not divide the A$1,500 testing budget between PMax and Display remarketing. PMax alone consumes the testing floor. Remarketing remains parked until its audience size, incremental role and separate budget are established.

### Platform sufficiency checks

| Check | Formula | Result | Status |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Meta delivery floor | A$20/day × 30 | A$600 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set |
| Raw Search enquiry CPL | A$4,246 last-30-day Search spend ÷ approximately 20 real leads | A$212.30 | Conservative upper-bound sensitivity only—not the Meta target-CPA anchor |
| Assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$212.30 × assumed 25%–40% lower-friction-event factor | A$53.08–A$84.92 | Assumption-based pending clean Meta Snapshot-request data |
| Provisional Meta target CPA | Conservative upper end of assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$84.92 | Planning anchor only—not a qualified-lead or profitable-acquisition target |
| Meta learning budget | 5 × A$84.92 | A$424.60 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set; A$600 delivery floor is controlling |
| Raw-enquiry-CPL upper-bound sensitivity | 5 × A$212.30 | A$1,061.50 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Sensitivity only; not used to set the proposed Meta budgets |
| PMax floor | A$50/day × 30 | A$1,500 per 30-day planning period | Only Scenario 3 passes |
| PMax under a 10% slice at current spend | 10% × A$4,246 | A$424.60 per 30-day planning period, or A$14.15/day | Fails the A$50/day floor by A$1,075.40 per 30-day planning period |
| Total budget needed for PMax to equal exactly 10% | A$1,500 ÷ 10% | A$15,000 per 30-day planning period | Well above the observed A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range |

The A$84.92 figure is an assumption-labeled event-level planning anchor, not a commercially defensible target CPA. The A$212.30 raw-enquiry CPL is retained only as an upper-bound sensitivity. A further caveat on the derivation: the "approximately 20 real leads" denominator is undifferentiated and may include certificate-intent conversions — "manual handling certificate" alone drew 55 clicks / 1.67 conversions in the last 30 days (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`) and those conversions are unclassified as individual versus organisational — so both A$212.30 and the derived A$84.92 anchor could be understated as costs per genuine corporate lead. Average contract value, contribution margin, qualified-lead rate, close rate and service capacity are unknown. Until those inputs and a clean conversion baseline exist:

- do not apply target CPA bidding;
- do not make unconditional pause or scale decisions;
- assess provisional Meta learning sufficiency against website `Lead`, while labelling A$84.92 as a Snapshot-path planning assumption rather than a blended observed CPA;
- replace the assumed range with observed Snapshot-request CPA as soon as clean Meta data is available;
- replace the planning anchor with a qualified-lead and contribution-margin-based ceiling as soon as CRM data is available.

## Proposed 90-day media plan

Committed 90-day KPIs are restricted to measurable leading indicators. Lead, qualified-lead, CPA and revenue outcomes establish baselines during this period rather than serving as commitments.

### Days 1–30 — Foundation and controlled build

| Work | Proposed actions | Committed leading indicators |
|---|---|---|
| Measurement | Inventory all 16 enabled conversion actions; isolate Consulting goals; demote newsletter and inappropriate soft actions; document browser/server deduplication; define `snapshot_request`, `direct_enquiry`, `call_connected`, `qualified_call`, `lead_qualified`, `proposal_sent` and `closed_won`; keep Snapshot booked/held as CRM stages, not platform events | 100% of active Consulting campaigns mapped to an approved conversion-goal set; zero newsletter signups used as primary Consulting optimisation events; test submissions reconcile across landing page, CRM, GA4 and ad platforms |
| Privacy | Implement CMP requirements and **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**; keep separate marketing consent; complete AU privacy review | Privacy review approved before paid-social or new landing-page launch; no health or injury fields in advertising forms |
| Landing page | Prepare a dedicated, navigation-reduced page with a two-step form and message-matched variants | One primary CTA per variant; all ads mapped to the intended variant; form validation and consent states pass QA |
| Search | Extend the resolved 30-day evidence with longer-history search-term and keyword-performance pulls; audit the existing 493 negatives; pull RSAs, assets, campaign settings and Quality Score components before restructuring; repair and de-duplicate Brand in place | Longer-history review completed; existing negatives audited before additions; Brand routing, destination and metrics verified after consolidation |
| Meta | Create isolated Pixel/Dataset scope, audiences and one consolidated prospecting build; creative specifications remain in Appendix D | Browser/server event deduplication test passes; audience exclusions and domain scope documented; campaign remains unpublished until privacy and tracking gates pass |
| PMax/remarketing | Keep both parked | No PMax activation before the gate checklist passes |

### Days 31–60 — Launch and baseline establishment

| Work | Proposed actions | Committed leading indicators |
|---|---|---|
| Search | Launch approved landing-page routing and tightly themed Exact/Phrase coverage; retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms | 100% of paid Search destinations use approved, relevant pages; weekly search-term review completed; no known product or physio bleed left unclassified |
| Meta | Launch one consolidated website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2. Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only. Enable Advantage+ placements; build visitor and engagement pools | Minimum A$20/day delivered; at least three materially distinct formats and five creatives available in the ad set, subject to Appendix D; Meta delivery, CTR, form-start and lead-entry CPA baselines recorded without declaring winners prematurely |
| Measurement | Validate GCLID/GBRAID/WBRAID/FBCLID and UTM capture; begin CRM-stage reconciliation | Source identifiers retained where available; lead-stage fields complete for all test leads; duplicate conversion count investigated and corrected |
| Governance | Review copy and form behaviour against AU and Meta policy | Every Snapshot placement includes “preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis”; zero personal-condition messaging |

### Days 61–90 — Diagnose, consolidate and decide

| Work | Proposed actions | Committed leading indicators |
|---|---|---|
| Search diagnosis | Compare clusters by query relevance, landing-page engagement, real-lead mix and emerging qualified-lead signals | Every active cluster assigned a diagnosis flag: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test; no unconditional kill/scale label without thresholds |
| Meta diagnosis | Compare creative concepts and audience delivery without fragmenting budget | Creative fatigue and format coverage reviewed; prospecting frequency maintained below 3.0 over seven days where reporting permits; audience overlap reviewed before adding ad sets |
| PMax decision | Evaluate readiness against the gate table below | Written activate/park decision; if activated, minimum A$1,500 per 30 days and documented PMax controls |
| Budget decision | Replace the assumed Snapshot-request CPA with clean observed event data and reconcile it to qualified-lead outcomes | Commercial target-CPA worksheet completed or explicitly marked not assessable; any increase proposed in increments no greater than 20%, followed by 3–5 days of observation |

### Conditional diagnosis thresholds

| Signal | Minimum evidence | Diagnosis—not automatic instruction |
|---|---|---|
| CPA greater than 3× an approved target | At least seven days and 20 clicks | Flag for pause review; inspect query intent, tracking, landing page and lead quality first |
| No conversions | At least A$100 spend or 50 clicks | Flag for diagnosis; do not pause solely on low-volume early data |
| Creative CTR more than 50% below an approved benchmark | At least 1,000 impressions | Flag creative for rebuild or replacement |
| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency 3–5 | Warning; inspect audience size and creative fatigue |
| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency above 5 | Fail diagnosis; do not assume budget alone is the cause |
| Creative fatigue | CTR decline greater than 20% across 14 days | Refresh candidate, subject to sufficient impressions |
| Search Quality Score | 5–6 warning; below 5 fail | Diagnose relevance, expected CTR and landing-page experience |
| Search CTR | At least 6.66% pass; 3–6.66% warning; below 3% fail | Apply only after comparable, clean campaign segmentation |
| Search CVR | At least 7.52% pass; 3–7.52% warning; below 3% fail | Use real primary conversions, not the current blended 26 |
| Search CPC | Up to A$5.26 pass; A$5.26–A$8 warning; above A$8 fail | Diagnose by keyword intent and qualified-lead value |

No campaign qualifies for a “scale” decision until CPA is below an approved target for at least two weeks, performance is stable and sufficient conversion evidence exists. The skill threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is not met by the current program.

## Assumption-labeled 12-month trajectory

These ranges are planning scenarios, not commitments. They assume the dedicated landing page launches, measurement is corrected, Meta receives adequate creative, privacy approval is obtained, service capacity is available, and budgets follow one of the proposed scenarios.

| Period | Conservative scenario | Base scenario | Expansion scenario |
|---|---|---|---|
| Months 1–3 | Search and Meta measurement baselines established; PMax parked | Scenario 2 launches with Search protected and Meta funded at A$600 per 30 days | Scenario 2 prepares PMax readiness while qualified-lead feedback begins |
| Months 4–6 | Search remains dominant; Meta continues only if delivery and lead-quality signals are interpretable | Meta receives up to 20% increases only after stable evidence; qualified-lead imports guide allocation | Scenario 3 activates PMax at A$1,500 per 30 days after all gates pass |
| Months 7–9 | Budget remains within the approved envelope informed by the A$3.0k–A$4.7k observed range; focus stays on efficiency and de-mixing | Total media operates around A$4,846 per 30 days, subject to commercial approval | Total media starts around A$6,346 per 30 days; PMax incrementality is tested against Search and Meta |
| Months 10–12 | PMax and paid remarketing remain parked if qualified-lead evidence is weak | Search/Meta allocation moves according to observed Snapshot-request and qualified-lead economics, subject to each ad set’s delivery and learning floors | Search/Meta/PMax allocation moves according to observed qualified-pipeline economics, subject to platform floors and incrementality evidence |

Possible annual media envelopes, assuming steady 30-day planning budgets, are approximately:

- Scenario 1: **A$50,952 per 12 planning periods**
- Scenario 2: **A$58,152 per 12 planning periods**
- Scenario 3: **A$76,152 per 12 planning periods**

These are budget envelopes, not spend, lead or revenue forecasts. They should not replace the verified historical anchor of approximately A$40,000 trailing 12 months.

