| Consumer/medical | Specific patient-treatment, diagnosis or symptom-treatment queries found in the report | Do not broadly exclude terms such as `pain` until actual queries and conversion paths are reviewed |
| CPR / first-aid bundle — conditional | `"cpr"` only if ErgoWorks confirms it does not deliver or partner on CPR; retain/review the existing `"first aid"` PHRASE and `[first aid and manual handling training]` EXACT controls rather than duplicating them | Ahrefs shows bundled demand at 150/month for `manual handling and cpr training` and 70/month for `manual handling and first aid training`, but keyword research is not a Search Terms Report. Hold any new negative until service scope is confirmed and an actual irrelevant query validates the match type |
| Vehicle ergonomics | `[driver ergonomic assessment]` if an actual irrelevant query appears; no duplicate additions for car/vehicle terms | The legacy list already has `car` BROAD, `[car ergonomic assessment]` EXACT and `[vehicle ergonomic assessment]` EXACT. Audit the over-broad `car` control and retain or narrow the exact controls; Ahrefs identifies car/vehicle/driver tails at 40/40/30 searches/month as out of scope |
| Assessment software / SaaS | `[ergonomic assessment software]` as the narrow candidate after Search Terms Report confirmation | The verified term has 40 searches/month and SaaS intent. Existing controls include `app` BROAD and several software-specific negatives, but not this exact phrase; audit the broad controls for overblocking and do not run this term as a positive ErgoAssess keyword |
| Free manual-handling variants | No duplicate addition while `free` BROAD remains live; after the audit, replace or retain only evidence-backed Exact/Phrase controls such as `[manual handling course free]` and specific `"free online"` query patterns | The campaign already has `free` BROAD and `[manual handling course free]` EXACT. Because Broad negatives can overblock and the approved Snapshot itself uses “free,” audit routing and duplication before any change; source any replacement from actual irrelevant Search Terms Report queries |
| Regulator/government informational | `"work safe australia"`, `"safe work"`, `"safework"`, `"workforce australia"`, `"high risk work licence"` as Exact/Phrase negatives at campaign level | These are non-commercial government-lookup queries matched into the DSA/generic groups with 0 conversions ("work safe australia" A$84.53 / 2 clicks / 0 conv). Note: a `worksafe` BROAD negative already exists in the 419-list — audit for duplication first, and verify the DSA-group leakage is a match-type/exact-competitor-keyword gap rather than a missing negative |
| Existing 493-negative audit | Full audit of the existing 419 campaign-level + 74 ad-group-level negatives | Review for (a) blockers against the approved care-sector, online, refresher and certificate trial sets, including `"aged care"`, `disability`, healthcare variants, `[online manual handling course]` and `[manual handling refresher course]`; (b) overblocking from generic single-token Broad negatives such as `certification`, `courses`, `advice`, `free`, `car` and `app`; (c) redundancy with the candidate themes above; and (d) stale person/name negatives — approximately 40+ individual first-name BROAD negatives (e.g. `adam`, `carol`, `emma`) — reviewed for retention versus removal |

#### Certificate-intent decision table

“Manual handling certificate” is the largest single search term by spend in the **2026-07-12 30-day top-60 pull** (A$364.86 / 55 clicks / 1.67 conv ≈ 3% CVR, versus “manual handling training” at ~13.6%), but certificate queries are not uniformly waste: “manual handling certificate online australia” produced **1.33 conversions from A$15.92**. The buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED** in current conversion data.

Ahrefs now verifies that this is a large demand pool rather than a fringe tail (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §2). The CPC figures below are approximate Ahrefs planning inputs, **not observed Google Ads CPC**:

| Verified certificate/course term | AU vol/mo | KD | Approx. Ahrefs CPC (planning A$) | Planning implication |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| `manual handling certificate` | **2,800** | 39 | A$1.00 | Commercial + transactional demand head; buyer type unclassified |
| `manual handling course` | **600** | 30 | A$1.00 | Part of the same certificate/course parent-topic pool; buyer type unclassified |
| `manual handling certificate online` | **150** | 43 | A$1.30 | Mixed online/certificate intent; Search-only and organisational qualification required |
| `accredited manual handling training` | **60** | 37 | A$0.90 | Makes accreditation a keyword-visible question; never imply accreditation without client evidence and sign-off |

The certificate + course head alone is approximately **3,400 searches/month**, with another 210/month across the verified online-certificate and accredited terms before close-variant overlap. This strengthens Option A because it tests a material pool, but volume does not classify the buyer as organisational. Do not blanket-exclude. Use these complementary controls as evidence permits:

| Option | Mechanics | Trade-off |
|---|---|---|
| **A — dedicated Certificate / Course mixed-intent split (RECOMMENDED, gated trial)** | Build as `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3`, Search-only, using Exact + Phrase and organisational qualification; route to the Manual Handling variant's certificate block. Do not build or publish until the client confirms whether ErgoWorks issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records | The verified approximately 3,400+ search/month pool makes the trial material rather than fringe, but buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED**. **Gated on the LP certificate block, accreditation and participant-record evidence, and client sign-off** (Appendix A); excluded from Meta |
| **B — exact-negative individual phrasings (can coexist with A)** | Exact negatives only on clearly individual searches such as personal-validity, personal-card or individual-accreditation phrasings; rely on the existing #1 organic blog ranking for excluded individual demand | Blocks only the exact clearly individual queries selected; it does not block broader corporate/online certificate queries unless those exact converting phrases are added in error |

“Accredited manual handling training” at **60 searches/month** makes accreditation a keyword-visible product question. ErgoWorks must confirm whether it provides accredited training, a statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records before the term, claim or landing-page block can publish; absent that evidence, do not bid on accreditation intent and do not imply equivalence. In either option, **Meta never targets certificate intent** (see Appendix D).

### Search bidding decision

Keep Maximize Conversions with no target CPA while measurement is repaired and a clean baseline develops. Do not recommend ECPC.

This explicitly conflicts with the ads-budget skill’s generic decision tree, which recommends Maximize Clicks below 30 conversions per month. The live campaign already uses Maximize Conversions, has a mature history, and records approximately 20 real leads per month plus misclassified primary actions. Moving to Maximize Clicks during tracking remediation could optimise for traffic rather than lead quality. The account-specific recommendation is therefore:

1. retain Maximize Conversions during remediation;
2. remove inappropriate primary signals;
3. observe a clean minimum 30-day baseline;
4. consider target CPA only after at least 30 clean conversions per month and stable qualified-lead economics;
5. consider target ROAS only after reliable revenue/contribution values and more than 50 appropriate conversions per month exist.

