### Conditional diagnosis thresholds

| Signal | Minimum evidence | Diagnosis—not automatic instruction |
|---|---|---|
| CPA greater than 3× an approved target | At least seven days and 20 clicks | Flag for pause review; inspect query intent, tracking, landing page and lead quality first |
| No conversions | At least A$100 spend or 50 clicks | Flag for diagnosis; do not pause solely on low-volume early data |
| Creative CTR more than 50% below an approved benchmark | At least 1,000 impressions | Flag creative for rebuild or replacement |
| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency 3–5 | Warning; inspect audience size and creative fatigue |
| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency above 5 | Fail diagnosis; do not assume budget alone is the cause |
| Creative fatigue | CTR decline greater than 20% across 14 days | Refresh candidate, subject to sufficient impressions |
| Search Quality Score | 5–6 warning; below 5 fail | Diagnose relevance, expected CTR and landing-page experience |
| Search CTR | At least 6.66% pass; 3–6.66% warning; below 3% fail | Apply only after comparable, clean campaign segmentation |
| Search CVR | At least 7.52% pass; 3–7.52% warning; below 3% fail | Use real primary conversions, not the current blended 26 |
| Search CPC | Up to A$5.26 pass; A$5.26–A$8 warning; above A$8 fail | Diagnose by keyword intent and qualified-lead value |

No campaign qualifies for a “scale” decision until CPA is below an approved target for at least two weeks, performance is stable and sufficient conversion evidence exists. The skill threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is not met by the current program.

