### Audience strategy

Meta job-title targeting is not the foundation.

| Audience | Proposed construction | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Broad/creative-qualified | **Approved service geography only**; broad adult organisational audience; creative and landing-page language identify WHS, HR, Facilities, Operations and workplace-program relevance | Initial consolidated prospecting. Australia-wide, Canberra/ACT, Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane expansion is wholly gated behind service-geography sign-off; no location is added merely because demand appears in research or account data |
| Interests | A limited, non-fragmented set around workplace safety, WHS, HR, occupational health, facilities and workplace management, subject to actual availability | Audience suggestions/test layer |
| Qualified-lead lookalikes | Consent-compatible lists of qualified leads, held consultations or closed-won customers; test 1%, then 3% and 5% only when seed quality and size are sufficient | Future scaling |
| Negative-audience layer (seed hygiene) | Exclude Search remarketing visitors who arrived via the certificate/individual-intent and competitor-conquesting terms (e.g. "alertforce", "go workplace training", "manual handling certificate" clicks) from any Meta lookalike **seed** list | Seeding lookalikes off blended Search converters would pull in individual/job-seeker profiles rather than corporate buyers; filter the seed before any lookalike build |
| Website retargeting | Consulting visitors, relevant service-page visitors, form starters and Snapshot visitors | Build from launch; fund later |
| Engagement retargeting | Approved video viewers and social engagers | Build from launch; fund later |
| Exclusions | Submitted leads, current clients, unrelated sister-brand users and inappropriate employee/patient audiences | Prospecting hygiene |

Audience language must describe organisational processes without implying that the viewer or a specific person has a medical condition. For example, focus on workplace assessment coverage, manual-task programs and prioritised implementation—not “Do you have back pain?” or equivalent personal-attribute framing.

### Meta budget and learning design

| Scenario | Meta budget | Proposed structure | Sufficiency |
|---|---:|---|---|
| Scenario 1 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes A$600 delivery floor and provisional A$424.60 learning check |
| Scenario 2 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes delivery and provisional learning checks while preserving the Search baseline |
| Scenario 3 | A$600 per 30 days; A$20/day | One prospecting ad set | Passes delivery and provisional learning checks; PMax separately receives A$1,500 |

The **provisional** learning check is **5 × A$84.92 = A$424.60** per ad set, based on the assumption-labeled Snapshot-request CPA anchor. It is not independently assessable until a real post-cleanup CPA exists. The independent **A$20/day delivery floor = A$600 per 30 days** is the only verified sufficiency check and therefore the controlling minimum.

Do not split A$600 across interests, broad, lookalike and retargeting ad sets. Each additional ad set would independently require at least A$20/day and at least 5× its event-level target CPA for learning.

Future scaling note (not launch): if the Meta budget later increases under the 20%-increment rule (Scenarios 2–3 trajectory), a geo-weighted or ACT-specific ad set may be considered — but only once volume supports a second ad set independently meeting the A$600 per 30 days / A$20 per day floor. The Canberra pocket is real but small (3 conversions); do not fragment the single consolidated ad set now.

### Meta launch-quality requirements

- At least five creatives in the launch ad set.
- At least three materially different formats where Appendix D production permits.
- Creative concepts must differ in angle, format, visual treatment, hook and headline—not merely minor variants.
- Target a pre-launch creative-diversity score of at least 8/10 under the concept, format, visual, hook and headline rubric.
- Keep video at no more than 15 seconds for Stories/Reels and no more than 30 seconds for Feed.
- Keep headlines under 40 characters and primary text under 125 characters where practical.
- Review creative fatigue every 14 days; a CTR decline greater than 20% is a diagnosis flag, subject to sufficient delivery.
- Aim for prospecting seven-day frequency below 3.0.
- The free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot must be B2B-only, limited in scope and accompanied by: **“Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.”**
- Do not use awards, Danone, logos, “ASX 100” or 5.0/63 reviews unless marked and cleared as **client sign-off required** before publication.

