The **provisional** learning check is **5 × A$84.92 = A$424.60** per ad set, based on the assumption-labeled Snapshot-request CPA anchor. It is not independently assessable until a real post-cleanup CPA exists. The independent **A$20/day delivery floor = A$600 per 30 days** is the only verified sufficiency check and therefore the controlling minimum.

Do not split A$600 across interests, broad, lookalike and retargeting ad sets. Each additional ad set would independently require at least A$20/day and at least 5× its event-level target CPA for learning.

Future scaling note (not launch): if the Meta budget later increases under the 20%-increment rule (Scenarios 2–3 trajectory), a geo-weighted or ACT-specific ad set may be considered — but only once volume supports a second ad set independently meeting the A$600 per 30 days / A$20 per day floor. The Canberra pocket is real but small (3 conversions); do not fragment the single consolidated ad set now.

### Meta launch-quality requirements

- At least five creatives in the launch ad set.
- At least three materially different formats where Appendix D production permits.
- Creative concepts must differ in angle, format, visual treatment, hook and headline—not merely minor variants.
